   "label": "High B2",
   "notes": [
    "Plan: curve Heroes out turns 2–5. Cap gives each one haste, vigilance and a counter, so every Hero attacks the turn it lands. Shared Animosity, Heroes' Podium and Door of Destinies turn a wide board into a lethal one; Herald's Horn, Jhoira and Kindred Discovery keep the hand full.",
    "Cut the off-plan pieces: the flash trio (Quicksilver, Speed, Vision), Hercules, the defensive ones (Patriot, Wasp), slow value (Tome, Gift of Immortality, Scarlet Witch), the dated removal (Destroy Evil, Make Your Move, Avenge, Hero's Blade), and the clunky artifacts and spells (Hulkbuster Armor, Avengers Quinjet, Raise the Palisade, Love on the Battlefield).",
    "Thor, Asgard's Avenger stays: every other source you control deals +1 damage to opponents and their stuff, so each attacking Hero hits for one more. The Mighty Thor, Jane Foster comes in too: a 3-mana flier whose attack trigger blinks a blocker out of the way or re-enters one of your own Heroes for another Cap trigger.",
    "Captain America, Wings of Freedom: flying, first strike, ward 1, and when he attacks every other Hero gets +X/+X where X is his toughness. Team Leader's counters grow that toughness, so the team pump grows every turn.",
    "Captain America's Shield on Wings of Freedom: +0/+8 makes his toughness 11+, so every other attacking Hero gets +11/+11 or more. The Shield is indestructible, gives vigilance and taps a blocker on each attack. On anyone else it's still a blocker-tapper.",
    "Hawkeye package: Kate Bishop (Hawkeye, Young Avenger) adds her power to all noncombat damage your sources deal to opponents and their stuff. Put Hawkeye's Bow on Clint (Hawkeye, Avenging Archer) and tap him to ping: Clint's ping and the Bow's trigger both get Kate's power, plus 1 more each with Thor, Asgard's Avenger out. With Kate at 3 power that's 5 to one opponent plus 5 to each opponent, every turn, without attacking.",
    "Equipment rule: an Equipment only earns a slot if it attaches itself or enables a combo. Three made it: Captain America's Shield (Wings of Freedom combo), Hawkeye's Bow (Kate engine), Vibranium Strike Gauntlets (attaches free, draws cards). Skipped Unstable Molecule Suit and Iron Man Armor as stat sticks; Mjölnir is on the buy list as an optional upgrade.",
    "Don't put the Bow and the Shield on the same creature: the Shield gives vigilance, so that creature never taps to attack.",
    "From the binder: Adarkar Wastes, Battlefield Forge and Shivan Reef (spares) replace a basic of each color; Captain America, Super-Soldier; Agent Phil Coulson, Monica Rambeau (front face of Monica Rambeau // Photon, Living Light) and The Mighty Thor, Jane Foster (all owned); Path to Exile and a Counterspell from the pile. Check Super-Soldier, Jane Foster and Path aren't already sleeved elsewhere.",
    "37 lands + 7 rocks (Herald's Horn and the cost reducers on top). Honor-Worn Shaku came out for Captain America's Shield.",
    "Nov 19, 2026: The Ozolith jumped to about $60, almost half the $150 cap on its own, so Thor Odinson (owned) takes its slot. Hawkeye, Young Avenger and Hawkeye's Bow are owned (Daredevil fold); Araña may still need checking.",
    "Nov 21, 2026 Hero round (all cards owned, need sleeving): IN Daredevil, Man Without Fear; Hawkeye, Trick Shot; Iron Man, Tony Stark; SP//dr, Piloted by Peni; Sensational Spider-Man; Wraith, Vicious Vigilante; Captain America, Unbowed; Marvel Boy, Noh-Varr; Spider-Woman, Stunning Savior; Matt Murdock, Justice Seeker; Captain America, Skybound. OUT Jocasta, Captain Mar-Vell, Shang-Chi and the Ten Rings, Photon, Mighty Marvel, Professor Hulk (goes to the oldest's Gamma deck), Captain America, Living Legend, Firebird, Blazing Ranger, Falcon and Redwing, Bastion Protector, Heroic Sacrifice, Dismantling Wave. Winter Soldier, Reborn Avenger stays (family's call).",
    "Why: Trick Shot pings for the number of Heroes every time a Hero enters, plus Kate's power and Thor's +1. Tony Stark's red spells make 2/1 flying Robot Hero tokens, which trigger Cap and Trick Shot. Cap's counters make every Hero modified, so SP//dr draws off every Hero that connects and Matt Murdock gives the whole team ward 1. Unbowed is the flash answer to wipes; Daredevil and Sensational keep the cards coming."
   ],
